---
import PlaygroundShell from '../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Simulate it" hint="80 chat requests with different output lengths arrive at a steady rate. One GPU replica serves them one decode step at a time. Switch the scheduler and the batch size and watch throughput, latency and idle slots.">
  <ol class="how">
    <li>Default: <b>continuous</b> batching, max batch 16, 4 requests per second. About 271 tokens/s, p95 latency about 16 s, 32% of slots idle. Switch to <b>Static</b>: about 114 tokens/s, p95 about 55 s and 74% idle, because every batch waits for its longest answer and the bars below show long gaps.</li>
    <li>In continuous mode step the max batch through 1, 4, 16, 32: tokens/s goes about 45, 141, 271, 302. Batch 64 gives exactly the same as 32 because the queue never holds more than 32. Look at the sweep table: p95 stops improving and slowly gets worse (16.0 s at 16, 17.4 s at 32) because every step is slower with more sequences in it.</li>
    <li>With batch 16 tick <b>Chunked prefill</b>: the longest step drops from about 415 ms to 61 ms (a 4,000 token prompt no longer freezes everyone else), for a small cost in throughput (about 265 tokens/s) and p95 (about 17.0 s).</li>
    <li>Set max batch 4 and queue limit <b>8</b> (continuous): about 51 of the 80 requests are rejected, but the ones accepted finish with p95 about 15 s instead of about 38 s. That is load shedding trading rejected requests for bounded latency.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="pg cbm" data-cbm>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Scheduler <select class="pg-in" data-mode><option value="continuous" selected>Continuous (iteration-level)</option><option value="static">Static (batch runs to the longest)</option></select></label>
      <label>Max batch size <select class="pg-in" data-batch><option>1</option><option>2</option><option>4</option><option>8</option><option selected>16</option><option>32</option><option>64</option></select></label>
      <label>Arrivals per second <input type="range" min="1" max="8" value="4" data-rate /> <b data-rateval>4</b></label>
      <label>Queue limit <select class="pg-in" data-queue><option value="0" selected>Unlimited</option><option value="8">8 waiting</option><option value="32">32 waiting</option></select></label>
      <label class="cbm-check"><input type="checkbox" data-chunk /> Chunked prefill (continuous only)</label>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--role-1)"><h3>Throughput</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-tps>0</span><span class="pg-note">generated tokens per second over the whole run</span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--role-3)"><h3>Latency p50 / p95</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-lat>0</span><span class="pg-note">arrival to last token, accepted requests</span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--role-4)"><h3>Idle slots</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-idle>0</span><span class="pg-note">batch slots that produced no token in a step</span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--role-2)"><h3>Longest step</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-longest>0</span><span class="pg-note">worst pause every running user felt</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-out" data-verdict aria-live="polite"></div>
    <h3>Slot occupancy over time</h3>
    <div class="cbm-bars" data-bars role="img" aria-label="Slot occupancy over time"></div>
    <p class="pg-note">Each bar is a slice of the run; its height is the share of batch slots that produced a token. Gaps mean the GPU waited for the longest sequence or for traffic.</p>
    <h3>Batch size sweep (same scheduler and traffic)</h3>
    <div class="cbm-sweep" data-sweep></div>
    <p class="pg-note">Assumptions: a decode step costs 20 ms (weights read once) plus 1 ms per sequence in the batch; prefill costs 1 ms per 10 prompt tokens; chunks are 256 tokens. 80 requests: 80% answer in 16 to 63 tokens, 20% in 200 to 399; 10% have a 2,000 to 3,999 token prompt. Seeded, so every run is identical. The constants are illustrative orders of magnitude, not a benchmark of any GPU. Static batching here returns every answer when the whole batch ends. KV memory limits are ignored; see the KV cache concept for that.</p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<script>
  interface Req { u: number; out: number; prompt: number; at: number }
  interface Opts { mode: 'static' | 'continuous'; maxBatch: number; queueLimit: number; chunked: boolean }
  const BASE = 20; const PER = 1; const CHUNK = 256; const N = 80; const SEED = 7; const COLS = 48;
  const MS_PER_S = 1000;
  const JITTER_RANGE = 1000; // arrival-gap draw is 0..999, scaled to 0..2x the mean gap
  const SHORT_PCT = 80; // % of requests with a short answer
  const OUT = { shortMin: 16, shortSpan: 48, longMin: 200, longSpan: 200 }; // answer length, tokens
  const LONG_PROMPT_EVERY = 10; // one request in this many has a long prompt
  const PROMPT = { longMin: 2000, longSpan: 2000, shortMin: 64, shortSpan: 900 }; // prompt length, tokens
  const PREFILL_TOK_PER_MS = 10; // prompt tokens prefilled per millisecond of step time
  const CLEAR_WIN = 1.2; // throughput ratio that counts as one scheduler clearly winning
  const IDLE_WARN_PCT = 50; // idle slot share that triggers the "over half empty" note
  const STALL_MS = 300; // a step this long counts as a stall
  function makeWorkload(n: number, seed: number) {
    let s = seed >>> 0;
    // LCG (Numerical Recipes constants)
    const next = () => { s = (Math.imul(s, 1664525) + 1013904223) >>> 0; return s >>> 8; };
    const w: { u: number; out: number; prompt: number }[] = [];
    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
      const u = next() % JITTER_RANGE; const r = next() % 100;
      const out = r < SHORT_PCT ? OUT.shortMin + (next() % OUT.shortSpan) : OUT.longMin + (next() % OUT.longSpan);
      const prompt = next() % LONG_PROMPT_EVERY === 0 ? PROMPT.longMin + (next() % PROMPT.longSpan) : PROMPT.shortMin + (next() % PROMPT.shortSpan);
      w.push({ u, out, prompt });
    }
    return w;
  }
  function arrivals(w: { u: number; out: number; prompt: number }[], rate: number): Req[] {
    let t = 0; const mean = MS_PER_S / rate;
    return w.map((r) => { t += Math.floor((r.u * 2 * mean) / JITTER_RANGE); return { ...r, at: t }; });
  }
  const pcost = (tok: number) => Math.floor((tok + PREFILL_TOK_PER_MS - 1) / PREFILL_TOK_PER_MS); // ms, rounded up
  function simulate(reqs: Req[], o: Opts) {
    const n = reqs.length; const fin = new Array<number>(n).fill(-1); const shed = new Array<boolean>(n).fill(false);
    let t = 0; let nx = 0; let steps = 0; let tokens = 0; let longest = 0;
    const queue: number[] = []; let act: { i: number; left: number }[] = []; const pre: { i: number; rem: number }[] = [];
    const trace: [number, number, number][] = [];
    const enq = () => { while (nx < n && reqs[nx].at <= t) { if (o.queueLimit && queue.length >= o.queueLimit) shed[nx] = true; else queue.push(nx); nx++; } };
    for (;;) {
      enq();
      if (!act.length && !pre.length && !queue.length) { if (nx >= n) break; t = reqs[nx].at; continue; }
      let extra = 0;
      const canAdmit = o.mode === 'continuous' || (!act.length && !pre.length);
      while (canAdmit && act.length + pre.length < o.maxBatch && queue.length) {
        const i = queue.shift()!;
        if (o.chunked && o.mode === 'continuous') pre.push({ i, rem: reqs[i].prompt });
        else { extra += pcost(reqs[i].prompt); act.push({ i, left: reqs[i].out }); }
      }
      let budget = o.chunked && o.mode === 'continuous' ? CHUNK : 0; const graduated: { i: number; rem: number }[] = [];
      while (budget > 0 && pre.length) {
        const take = Math.min(budget, pre[0].rem); pre[0].rem -= take; budget -= take; extra += pcost(take);
        if (pre[0].rem === 0) graduated.push(pre.shift()!);
      }
      const dt = BASE + PER * act.length + extra; let live = 0;
      for (const a of act) { if (a.left > 0) { a.left--; tokens++; live++; } }
      trace.push([t, dt, live]);
      t += dt; steps++; if (dt > longest) longest = dt;
      if (o.mode === 'continuous') act = act.filter((a) => { if (a.left === 0) { fin[a.i] = t; return false; } return true; });
      else if (act.every((a) => a.left === 0)) { for (const a of act) fin[a.i] = t; act = []; }
      for (const g of graduated) act.push({ i: g.i, left: reqs[g.i].out });
    }
    const lat: number[] = []; for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) if (fin[i] >= 0) lat.push(fin[i] - reqs[i].at);
    lat.sort((a, b) => a - b);
    const pct = (q: number) => (lat.length ? lat[Math.floor(((lat.length - 1) * q) / 100)] : 0);
    return {
      done: lat.length, shed: shed.filter(Boolean).length, tokens, steps, makespan: t, trace,
      tps: t ? Math.floor((tokens * MS_PER_S) / t) : 0, p50: pct(50), p95: pct(95),
      idle: steps ? Math.floor(100 - (100 * tokens) / (steps * o.maxBatch)) : 0, longest,
    };
  }
  const sec = (ms: number) => (ms / MS_PER_S).toFixed(1) + ' s';
  const SIZES = [1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32, 64];
  const base = makeWorkload(N, SEED);

  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-cbm]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = <T extends HTMLElement>(s: string) => root.querySelector<T>(s)!;
    const sel = (s: string) => q<HTMLSelectElement>(s).value;
    const bars = q('[data-bars]'); const sweep = q('[data-sweep]');
    const barEls: HTMLElement[] = [];
    for (let i = 0; i < COLS; i++) { const b = document.createElement('span'); b.className = 'cbm-bar'; bars.appendChild(b); barEls.push(b); }
    const rows: { row: HTMLElement; fill: HTMLElement; text: HTMLElement }[] = [];
    SIZES.forEach((sz) => {
      const row = document.createElement('div'); row.className = 'cbm-row';
      const name = document.createElement('span'); name.className = 'pg-mono'; name.textContent = 'batch ' + sz;
      const track = document.createElement('span'); track.className = 'cbm-track';
      const fill = document.createElement('span'); fill.className = 'cbm-fill'; track.appendChild(fill);
      const text = document.createElement('span'); text.className = 'pg-mono';
      row.append(name, track, text); sweep.appendChild(row); rows.push({ row, fill, text });
    });
    let raf = 0;
    function opts(batch: number): Opts {
      return { mode: sel('[data-mode]') as Opts['mode'], maxBatch: batch, queueLimit: Number(sel('[data-queue]')), chunked: q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-chunk]').checked };
    }
    function verdict(r: ReturnType<typeof simulate>, o: Opts, reqs: Req[]) {
      const other = simulate(reqs, { ...o, mode: o.mode === 'static' ? 'continuous' : 'static' });
      const notes: string[] = [];
      if (o.maxBatch === 1) notes.push('Batch size 1 is no batching: every step reads all the weights for a single sequence, so the GPU is busy but moves only about ' + r.tps + ' tokens/s.');
      else if (o.mode === 'static' && other.tps > r.tps * CLEAR_WIN) notes.push('Static batching: ' + r.idle + '% of slots idle. Short answers sit finished inside the batch until the longest one ends. Continuous batching would give ' + other.tps + ' tokens/s and p95 ' + sec(other.p95) + ' on the same traffic.');
      else if (o.mode === 'continuous' && r.tps > other.tps * CLEAR_WIN) notes.push('Continuous batching refills a slot the moment a sequence finishes: ' + r.tps + ' tokens/s against ' + other.tps + ' for static batching, p95 ' + sec(r.p95) + ' against ' + sec(other.p95) + '.');
      else notes.push('At this load the two schedulers are close, so the scheduler is not what limits you.');
      if (r.shed > 0) notes.push(r.shed + ' of ' + reqs.length + ' requests were rejected by the queue limit; the accepted ones have bounded latency.');
      if (o.mode === 'continuous' && r.idle >= IDLE_WARN_PCT) notes.push('Over half the slots are empty: the queue is shorter than the batch, so a bigger max batch buys nothing here.');
      if (r.longest >= STALL_MS) notes.push('Longest step ' + r.longest + ' ms: a long prompt stalled every running user' + (o.mode === 'continuous' ? '; chunked prefill would spread it out.' : '.'));
      return notes.join(' ');
    }
    function draw() {
      raf = 0;
      const rate = Number(q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-rate]').value);
      q('[data-rateval]').textContent = String(rate);
      const mode = sel('[data-mode]'); const chunk = q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-chunk]');
      chunk.disabled = mode !== 'continuous';
      const reqs = arrivals(base, rate); const o = opts(Number(sel('[data-batch]')));
      const r = simulate(reqs, o);
      q('[data-tps]').textContent = r.tps + ' tokens/s';
      q('[data-lat]').textContent = sec(r.p50) + ' / ' + sec(r.p95);
      q('[data-idle]').textContent = r.idle + '%';
      q('[data-longest]').textContent = r.longest + ' ms';
      q('[data-verdict]').textContent = verdict(r, o, reqs);
      const occ = new Array<number>(COLS).fill(0); const w = r.makespan / COLS;
      for (const [t0, dt, live] of r.trace) {
        let a = t0; const end = t0 + dt;
        while (a < end) { const c = Math.min(COLS - 1, Math.floor(a / w)); const stop = Math.min(end, (c + 1) * w); occ[c] += ((stop - a) * live) / o.maxBatch; a = stop > a ? stop : end; }
      }
      barEls.forEach((b, i) => { const v = Math.min(1, occ[i] / w); b.style.height = Math.max(2, Math.round(v * 100)) + '%'; });
      bars.setAttribute('aria-label', 'Slot occupancy over time. Average ' + (100 - r.idle) + ' percent of slots busy.');
      const sw = SIZES.map((sz) => simulate(reqs, opts(sz)));
      const top = Math.max(...sw.map((x) => x.tps), 1);
      sw.forEach((x, i) => {
        rows[i].fill.style.width = Math.round((100 * x.tps) / top) + '%';
        rows[i].text.textContent = x.tps + ' tok/s · p95 ' + sec(x.p95) + (x.shed ? ' · shed ' + x.shed : '');
        rows[i].row.classList.toggle('cur', SIZES[i] === o.maxBatch);
      });
    }
    function schedule() { if (!raf) raf = requestAnimationFrame(draw); }
    root.addEventListener('input', schedule); root.addEventListener('change', schedule);
    draw();
  });
</script>
<style is:global>
  .playground .cbm-check { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; }
  .playground .cbm-bars { display: flex; align-items: flex-end; gap: 2px; height: 72px; padding: 4px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 8px; background: var(--surface); }
  .playground .cbm-bar { flex: 1 1 0; min-width: 0; background: var(--role-1); border-radius: 2px 2px 0 0; transition: height .25s; }
  .playground .cbm-sweep { display: grid; gap: 6px; }
  .playground .cbm-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: max-content minmax(60px, 1fr); gap: 4px 10px; align-items: center; padding: 4px 6px; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid transparent; }
  .playground .cbm-row.cur { border-color: var(--accent); background: var(--accent-soft); }
  .playground .cbm-row > .pg-mono:last-child { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
  .playground .cbm-track { display: block; height: 10px; background: var(--surface-2); border-radius: 5px; overflow: hidden; }
  .playground .cbm-fill { display: block; height: 100%; background: var(--role-1); transition: width .25s; }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .playground .cbm-bar, .playground .cbm-fill { transition: none; } }
</style>
